---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { stats } from '../lib/data';
---

<Base title="About" description="What Seichi Atlas is, why it exists, and the rules that keep it accurate and respectful.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="micro">About</p>
      <h1 class="display-lg" style="margin:.7rem 0 1rem;">An atlas for anime pilgrims</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Seichi Atlas turns scattered Japanese-language fan notes into a structured database of
        real anime locations: coordinates, travel time from Tokyo, whether you can actually visit,
        and when the information was last checked.
      </p>

      <h2>Why coordinates matter</h2>
      <p>
        Search results will happily tell you <em>that</em> a stairway appears in a famous film.
        They rarely tell you <em>where</em> it is, how long the train takes, or that the site has
        since been closed. This site carries the facts that answer those questions, and nothing more:
        no plot summaries, no reviews, no rankings. Just places, mapped.
      </p>

      <h2>How we keep it honest</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every location has a <strong>last-verified date</strong>, shown on the page.</li>
        <li>Every claim carries <strong>confidence</strong>: confirmed, likely, or disputed.</li>
        <li>Every appearance links to its <strong>source</strong>.</li>
        <li>Closed and off-limits sites are kept on the map with a reason, not deleted.</li>
        <li>Private homes are never given exact coordinates.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data</h2>
      <p>
        Factual data (coordinates, addresses, access) is released under CC BY-SA 4.0 where
        applicable. Site text and the route tooling keep normal copyright. Map data comes from
        OpenStreetMap and carries the ODbL share-alike requirement.
      </p>

      <p class="mono" style="color:var(--text-faint); font-size:.8rem;">
        Current build: {stats.works} series · {stats.locations} locations · Kanto day-trip edition
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  .prose h2 { margin: 2.4rem 0 0.8rem; font-size: 1.35rem; }
  .prose p { margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .prose ul { margin: 0 0 1.4rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .prose li::marker { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
